      "id": "lettering_0126",
      "source_lettering_item_id": "lettering_0126",
      "role": "caption",
      "text_by_locale": {
        "source": "Wilcox still lived alone in the Fleur-de-Lys Building in Thomas Street — a hideous Victorian imitation of seventeenth-century Breton architecture, flaunting its stuccoed front amidst the lovely colonial houses on the ancient hill, under the very shadow of the finest Georgian steeple in America."
      },
      "suggested_placement": {
        "x": 0.0283203125,
        "y": 0.013671875,
