    {
      "id": "lettering_0127",
      "source_lettering_item_id": "lettering_0127",
      "role": "caption",
      "text_by_locale": {
        "source": "I found him at work in his rooms, and at once conceded from the specimens scattered about that his genius is indeed profound and authentic. He will, I believe, some time be heard from as one of the great decadents; he has crystallised in clay, and will one day mirror in marble, those nightmares and phantasies which Arthur Machen evokes in prose and Clark Ashton Smith makes visible in verse and in painting."
      },
      "suggested_placement": {
